<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hans Christian Andersen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1805">1805</a>–<a href="/years/1875">1875</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hans Christian Andersen was a Danish writer, born in Odense, best known for his fairy tales, among them &quot;The Little Mermaid&quot;, &quot;The Ugly Duckling&quot;, &quot;The Emperor's New Clothes&quot; and &quot;The Snow Queen&quot;. He also wrote novels, plays, poems and travel books. His tales, published from 1835, have been translated into more languages than almost any other works of literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hans-christian-andersen.jpg" alt="Hans Christian Andersen" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thora Hallager · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HCA_by_Thora_Hallager_1869_crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
